      "description": "Watch Heerenveen vs AZ Alkmaar highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 6, 2026. The Eredivisie clash between SC Heerenveen and AZ Alkmaar on September 6, 2026, delivered a rollercoaster of emotions for the 22,164 fans in attendance. Both sides displayed an attacking philosophy that ensured a high-scoring affair and dramatic momentum shifts throughout the afternoon. A Fast-Paced Opening Exchange The contest ignited early as AZ Alkmaar found the breakthrough in the 7th minute. Ro-Zangelo Daal clinical finish, set up by a precise pass from Wouter Goes , gave the visitors an early platform. However, SC Heerenveen refused to be intimidated and fought back into the contest. Their persistence paid off in the 21st minute when Nolhan Courtens found the back of the net following an assist from Dylan Vente , restoring parity and energizing the home crowd. Building on their equalizer, the hosts took control of the narrative before the break. In the 30th minute, Ringo Meerveld unleashed a shot that took a significant deflection, tricking the goalkeeper and nestling into the net to make it 2-1. Heerenveen entered the tunnel at halftime with the momentum, but the second half would prove that the visitors had plenty of fight left. AZ Mount a Clinical Comeback As the second half progressed, tactical substitutions from the AZ Alkmaar bench began to turn the tide. In the 69th minute, Mexx Meerdink produced a moment of individual brilliance, firing a powerful left-footed strike from outside the box into the goal to level the score at 2-2. The assist came from Valdemar Byskov , signaling a shift in dominance as the visitors began to pin Heerenveen back. With only seven minutes of normal time remaining, the final blow was struck. Ayoub Oufkir , who had only been on the pitch for sixty seconds, showcased incredible composure to lob the goalkeeper with his left foot after being played through by Meerdink . Despite late pressure from Heerenveen and several dangerous headers from Roberts Uldrikis that required sharp saves from Jari De Busser , AZ Alkmaar held firm to claim a hard-fought 3-2 victory."
